<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  The logo as the splash screen should draw it: rounded, and whole.

  WHAT THE SPLASH DOES TO ITS ICON
  It shows the icon inside a CIRCLE whose diameter is 2/3 of the icon (Android documents 192 dp for a
  288 dp icon without background; the androidx compat library applies the same rule below Android 12).
  Anything outside that circle is clipped.

  WHY NOT `ic_launcher_foreground` AS IT IS
  Its square is barely rounded (about 3 % of its side): on the home screen the launcher mask does the
  rounding. The splash has no such mask. The first fix inset that square by 16 %, computed against a
  circle as wide as the whole canvas — but the visible circle is 2/3 of it, so the corners still
  overflowed by about 6.6 dp and were clipped by a shallow arc that read as cut corners (seen on the
  Galaxy S9, 2026-10-05).

  WHAT IS USED INSTEAD
  `splash_logo`, built by `tools/make-splash-logo.py` from the launcher artwork: the same square,
  with its corners rounded at 13 % of its side — the rounding of the SMS Tech logo, so the apps open
  alike. A rounded square of side s reaches 0.65 s from its centre; to stay within the circle
  (radius 1/3 of the icon), s may be at most 51 % of the icon. An inset of 26 % per side gives 48 %,
  so the farthest point sits 4.7 dp inside the circle on a 288 dp icon.

  `mipmap/ic_launcher` is deliberately left alone: the launcher masks it itself.
-->
<inset xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    android:drawable="@drawable/splash_logo"
    android:inset="26%" />
